        "description": "Company Overview\n \n\n\n\n Caprae Capital Partners is a lower middle\\-market private equity and acquisitions platform supported by Al led by Kevin Hong \\- a serial founder who scaled two tech ventures to $31M ARR (FinTech) and $7M (Entertainment) revenue.\n \n\n\n\n Today, Caprae is one of the fastest\\-scaling platforms in the lower\\-middle\\-market M\\&A and ETA ecosystem, combining an international research engine, a full\\-stack deal sourcing arm, and a rapidly expanding tech layer.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n YTD, Caprae's services divisions have completed $50M worth of transaction value and is expected to exceed $150M in Q1 \\& Q2 of 2026 after launching in January of 2025\\. We're looking for those who are looking to take PE to the next level.\n \n\n\n\n Caprae is growing incredibly fast and is expected to grow 25% MoM for most of 2026 and we need someone who is crazy about building a rocket ship with us with the right talent.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Role Description\n \n\n\n\n The Full Stack Developer will be responsible for building and maintaining the technology layer that powers Caprae Capital's deal sourcing and AI\\-driven research engine. This includes developing and improving features across full\\-stack applications, contributing to AI/ML development workflows, and working seamlessly across backend and frontend systems. The role will also involve managing deployments on Ubuntu servers, maintaining already\\-deployed services, and moving quickly to ship solutions and resolve issues as they arise, supporting Caprae's rapidly scaling tech infrastructure across its M\\&A and ETA platform.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Key Responsibilities\n \n\n\n* Build and improve features across full\\-stack apps.\n* Contribute to AI/ML development workflows.\n* Ship quickly and address issues as they come up.\n* Work across both backend and frontend.\n* What we look for\n* Full\\-stack development experience.\n* Solid understanding of databases (schema design, queries, and data handling).\n* Familiarity with FastAPI, Flask, Node.js, and JavaScript.\n* Experience with the React framework.\n* Comfort working with Ubuntu servers and handling deployments.\n* Understanding of already\\-deployed services and how to maintain them.\n* Strong problem\\-solving skills and the ability to pick up new tools quickly.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Full\\-time, remote position.",
