    "linkedin:c96820b3470b7c0a114ba5ea": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Web Developer (Python/Django)",
        "company": "Sundayy",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467061604",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n National Journal is a leading research and insights organization dedicated to providing comprehensive and reliable information to policymakers, government officials, and industry leaders. With a history spanning nearly 50 years, our organization has established itself as one of Washington's most trusted media brands, renowned for delivering in\\-depth analysis, data\\-driven insights, and expert commentary on government affairs, politics, and policy issues. Our mission is to empower decision\\-makers with the intelligence, connections, and tools they need to navigate the complexities of Washington and beyond. We foster a culture of intellectual rigor, innovation, and service, striving to produce high\\-quality journalism and digital products that inform and influence public discourse.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking a mid\\-level Django/Python Web Developer to join our dynamic digital team. In this role, you will be instrumental in building, maintaining, and enhancing web\\-based tools and platforms that serve our extensive audience of government affairs professionals, policy advocates, and political enthusiasts. Your work will directly impact how our users access election data, demographic information, government directories, and other vital resources. You will collaborate with cross\\-functional teams to develop scalable, efficient, and user\\-friendly applications, supporting our mission of delivering timely and relevant content. The ideal candidate will have a strong foundation in Python and Django, experience working on medium to large projects, and a passion for working with data and modern development practices. This position offers full\\-time remote work opportunities within the United States, with flexibility for in\\-person collaboration in Washington, DC, for local candidates.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n* At least 1 year of professional web development experience using Python, preferably with Django framework\n* Proficiency in writing clean, semantic HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n* Experience with Git version control system\n* Familiarity with front\\-end frameworks (e.g., Vue.js, TypeScript) is a plus\n* Hands\\-on experience with LLM\\-based coding assistants such as Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor\n* Knowledge of database systems like PostgreSQL, MySQL, and working with APIs\n* Experience maintaining and working with large datasets and complex codebases\n* Understanding of software development best practices, including automated testing, peer code review, and documentation\n* Ability to work collaboratively in an Agile environment and communicate effectively with team members and stakeholders\n* Interest or experience in government data, elections, or political analysis is highly desirable\n* Experience with additional technologies such as Docker, Elasticsearch, Jenkins, or cloud platforms like Microsoft Azure is a plus\n\n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Design, develop, test, and deploy web applications and tools built with Django and Python to support our digital platform\n* Maintain and enhance large datasets in PostgreSQL, MySQL, and through various APIs, ensuring data integrity and accessibility\n* Support the internal content management system, Ada, by implementing improvements and new features\n* Create automation tools and support other product teams in streamlining their workflows, leveraging AI technologies when appropriate\n* Participate in code reviews, write automated tests, and ensure high\\-quality code standards across projects\n* Stay informed about emerging trends in software development, AI integration, and workflow automation to bring innovative ideas to the team\n* Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other developers to deliver features aligned with project goals and deadlines\n* Contribute to documentation, technical specifications, and knowledge sharing within the team\n* Assist in troubleshooting and resolving technical issues promptly to ensure platform stability and performance\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Competitive salary starting at $100,000, commensurate with experience\n* Full\\-time remote work options within the U.S., with in\\-person work available in Washington, DC (3 days/week)\n* Flexible work schedules to promote work\\-life balance\n* Health, dental, and vision insurance options\n* Generous paid time off and holidays\n* Professional development opportunities, including training in emerging technologies and frameworks\n* Access to a collaborative and innovative work environment focused on impactful projects\n* Participation in a mission\\-driven organization committed to public service and intellectual rigor\n\n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n National Journal is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex (including gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other protected class under applicable law. We encourage individuals of all backgrounds to apply and join our team. We may utilize artificial intelligence tools during the recruitment process to assist with application review and assessment, but final hiring decisions are made by our human team members, ensuring fairness and equity throughout the process.",
